 "_note": "Each vendor's identity read for check-real and the keeper: a tools-RPC method from the plugin's own `describe` at the pinned release (evals-plugins.json), 20 Nov 2026, that REALLY CALLS THE VENDOR (calls_vendor). `expect` is a list of groups, ALL must hold, each group any-of: a path from the RPC answer, `:type` (string = non-empty, array, number, object, true, email = an address on a line of its own or an `email: <address>` line, profile = a non-empty text that does not open with an error word). `~json` after a key parses that string as JSON first. ashby/elevenlabs/wisprflow/gws probes only read whether a credential is held and call nothing, so they are NOT used. Edit here, never in the scripts. `inner` lists the tool actions a probe reads through the host (X: `x_probe needs x_get_users_me`); the check session allows `action` plus these and nothing else. A read a probe turns out to need that is not listed is learned once from the PERMISSION_DENIED message, only when describe lists it as a read of the same plugin, and added to a NEW session, never a wildcard.",
